    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Sherry FitzGerald Davitt & Davitt are delighted to present this exceptional A1-rated, fully furnished four-bedroom detached bungalow with study, ideally positioned overlooking a large green within the exclusive Clog Na Léinn development in the picturesque village of Collinstown, Co. Westmeath. Combining cutting-edge energy efficiency with contemporary style, this turnkey home is ready for immediate occupation and has been thoughtfully designed to offer spacious, comfortable family living in one of the Midlands' most scenic locations, just moments from the crystal-clear waters of Lough Lene.\n\nA striking entrance hallway with an impressive double-height ceiling sets the tone for the accommodation, leading into a bright and spacious open-plan living area. The contemporary kitchen is fitted with high-quality modern units, granite worktop and a matching central island, seamlessly flowing into the dining and living areas. French doors open onto a private south-facing rear garden and patio, allowing natural light to flood the home.\n\nThe ground floor offers three generously proportioned bedrooms, including one with an en-suite bathroom, together with a stylish family bathroom, utility area, guest cloakroom and plant room, all finished to an exceptional standard.\n\nThe first floor is dedicated to a superb master suite featuring fitted wardrobes, a spacious ensuite and a separate study/dressing room. This versatile additional room is perfectly suited as a home office, nursery, playroom, hobby room or private retreat, adapting to changing family needs.\n\nBuilt to the highest modern standards, the property boasts an impressive A1 Energy Rating and benefits from underfloor heating throughout, a NIBE Exhaust Air Heat Pump system and roof-mounted solar panels. Together, these advanced systems deliver outstanding energy efficiency, lower running costs and exceptional year-round comfort while creating a healthy and sustainable indoor environment.\n\nExternally, the home enjoys ample private parking to the front and a beautifully maintained south-facing rear garden offering excellent privacy and sunshine throughout the day. Overlooking an attractive communal green, the property enjoys a peaceful setting that is ideal for families.\n\nLocated in the heart of Ireland's Hidden Heartlands, Clog Na Léinn offers the perfect balance of village life and modern convenience. The renowned Lough Lene, Ireland's first Blue Flag inland lake, is just a short distance away, providing opportunities for swimming, kayaking, fishing and scenic walks. Collinstown itself offers a welcoming community with a primary school, crèche, local shops and everyday amenities all within easy reach, while Mullingar, Castlepollard and the wider Midlands region are conveniently accessible. Serviced with the New TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays.\n\nSpecial Features\nA1 BER energy-efficient detached family home\nFour spacious bedrooms plus dedicated study/dressing room\nThree fully fitted bathrooms including two ensuites\nBright open-plan kitchen, dining and living room\nContemporary high-specification finish throughout\nNIBE Exhaust Air Heat Pump system\nSolar photovoltaic (PV) power generation system\nExceptional energy efficiency and low running costs\nMechanical ventilation and balanced indoor climate control\nUtility room and plant room\nLocated in the heart of Collinstown village\nMinutes from Lough Lene, Irelands first Blue Flag inland lake\nPeaceful countryside setting within Irelands Hidden Heartlands\nIdeal family home\nSouth facing private rear garden with patio\nTarmac drive offering ample parking\nFully furnished turn key property\nClose to primary school and Creche\nClose to local shop & pubs\nClose to Pitch and Putt and Gym\nCollinstown is serviced by TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays."
      },
